{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics","id":820426,"title":"Spontaneous Werewolf Genetics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-31T10:36:56-08:00","id":820426,"title":"Spontaneous Werewolf Genetics","content":"So the Werewolf larp gamma is out and it has a new thing it where because nature is trying to equal itself because the Garou are losing random people are gaining a mutation where they have the potential to be wherewolves. Basically if the character gets bitten by a werewolf it triggers this mutation and turns the character into a Garou. I'm mostly interested in what the people who play the larp think of this new thing. Personally I think it's stupid and goes against the whole story of what the Garou are (perhaps I would be more accepting of it if it was some kind of forbidden rite or something) and personally hope that it never is added to the Werewolf game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:42:07-08:00","id":820467,"title":"","content":"Well, first of all we must take into account that a lot of werewolf fans dislike WtA for lacking 'true' werewolves. The frenzied monsters that are turned against their will and have to fight back the beast. This rule seems to harken to that.<br /> <br /> However, regardless of the above paragraph, I don't like this change. Mostly, because it conflicts so strongly with the themes of WtA.<br /> <br /> WtA is very much a game of community, the garou have their own culture and their own laws. Their own traditions and their own heroes and villains. A huge part of the game is the bonds of family between kinfolk, tribe and pack. To all of this, the biting angle conflicts strongly. The character is no longer born as garou, and so truly never had a chance with humanity or wolves in the first place. To be bitten is to be forced into that life from a perfectly mundane human life, and that very much doesn't fit the themes of the garou. They take pride in what they are, some even think they are above humans. Plus, their laws put a huge focus on not revealing themselves to the public. Lost Cubs are all ready a hard thing to deal with in regards to the Veil, think of a randomly bitten human.<br /> <br /> In addition, biting humans to increase the forces is something I could see BSDs doing easily, not as much Gaian garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T11:46:03-08:00","id":820469,"title":"","content":"One thing I've disliked for a while is the fact that NOTHING Can allow a normal human however worthy to become garou, but in spite of the aforementioned, I accept sometimes life isnt fair, and this creates some fascinating story arcs.<br /> <br /> Id agree this kind of major change is something to VERY CAREFULLY Consider...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 01-31-2016, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:01:34-08:00","id":820477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820469#post820469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've disliked for a while is the fact that NOTHING Can allow a normal human however worthy to become garou, but in spite of the aforementioned, I accept sometimes life isnt fair, and this creates some fascinating story arcs.<br /> <br /> Id agree this kind of major change is something to VERY CAREFULLY Consider...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always seen it as that regular humans both wouldn't cut it as a garou, and that they are more free than the garou.<br /> <br /> Garou are a combination of three aspects, human spirit and wolf. For those three to exist as well as they do, having to grow up with it makes sense. But more on the latter point, think of a Lost Cub who doesn't want to be a garou. Despite all the talk to them, they don't want to take part in the war at all.<br /> <br /> But, they can never not be garou, no matter how hard they try to control their Rage, it still causes them to be angry. And even if they become ronin, there are the BSDs and any werewolf hunters to consider. Humans don't have that burden.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:39:13-08:00","id":820506,"title":"","content":"It's a bit more complex than just, &quot;now Garou can bite humans, who might become Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> Part of the metaplot of the new BNS game is that after [big battle resolving the Revised metaplot stuff that's still pretty vague] werewolf bloodlines that have been spiritually dormant are reawakening. Basically, people that are multiple generations removed from their closest Garou ancestor who lost their spiritual connection to Gaia... suddenly have it back. Some of them are now fully kin and capable of having new Garou children, and some are potential Garou, waiting for a trigger.<br /> <br /> I think it's a bit early to judge it, but I don't think it's an inherently bad move. I can see why people don't like it, but there's a lot in there that's pretty important to moving WtA forward: scrapping the &quot;dying race&quot; aspect, expanding the Tribes to get away from cultural stereotypes without retcons, providing new directions for in-game conflict, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that BNS is focused on LARP based play, which for WtA can have a very different focus than TT based play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T12:47:43-08:00","id":820510,"title":"","content":"That is true but I feel that the justification they use is a horrible tack on to the game. It's long since been a thing that Garou can be born to normal families because they have some ancestry that has stayed dormant for a generations and that's all it really needed. The bite thing is unnecessary at best and a horrible Hollywood tack on at worst. It changes the very nature of what werewolves in this setting are and how they relate to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T13:01:05-08:00","id":820519,"title":"","content":"It goes against the original conception of the game. I like the trope it is trying to emulate, but it is best done by emphasizing aspects of the existing mythos like Ronin, Lost Cubs, and Lunatics. Many months ago, I wrote a series of posts about how the game can emulate the traditional werewolf tropes in cinema, literature, and folklore. It's not that hard. It's just that those aspects were ignored in the setting and various guides. One of those ideas was that Garou could attempt to awaken or trigger the dormant change by biting the Lost Cub or Lunatic perhaps as part of a Rite. It's certainly more elegant than creating an entire new system of birthing Garou and doesn't invalidate how things were portrayed in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:18:37-08:00","id":820599,"title":"","content":"I find a setting in that pretty much every person could be a garou is not the WtA I love. Even with an explanation, like the vague thing that happens and destroys most caerns and changes the whole world (of the garou) and all that I find the changes lead to a new game that should clearly be a new Setting.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see how this shifted focus and the problem that virtually anyone could be a garou could lead to interesting stories and such. It also addresses the problem I have with W20, regarding not knowing of a child is garou, when this circumstances are a recent development, not presented as fact since the Dawn Times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:48:02-08:00","id":820619,"title":"","content":"<b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> changed the matter of \u201cwhere do werewolves come from?\u201d in its second edition in order to downplay the breeding issue: the protagonists are always wolf-bloods or children of \u201cwolf-bloods\u201d; but a human can become wolf-blooded by having a bad encounter with a werewolf or spirit. It's a neat idea, and one that I really like. But part of the reason it was done was to help distance WtF from WtA. I'm not sure how I feel about WtA following WtF's lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T15:55:26-08:00","id":820621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820599#post820599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find a setting in that pretty much every person could be a garou is not the WtA I love. Even with an explanation, like the vague thing that happens and destroys most caerns and changes the whole world (of the garou) and all that I find the changes lead to a new game that should clearly be a new Setting.<br /> <br /> That said, I can see how this shifted focus and the problem that virtually anyone could be a garou could lead to interesting stories and such. It also addresses the problem I have with W20, regarding not knowing of a child is garou, when this circumstances are a recent development, not presented as fact since the Dawn Times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, one more issue comes to mind, and that;s &quot;good luck with that first tenet of the litany if you don't know if anyone is really Garou or not.&quot; I mean, above and beyond the usual possibility of disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T16:49:11-08:00","id":820641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820621#post820621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, one more issue comes to mind, and that;s &quot;good luck with that first tenet of the litany if you don't know if anyone is really Garou or not.&quot; I mean, above and beyond the usual possibility of disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before any of that is, we have to first figure out whether pre-change homid garou are raised unaware of their natures, or not. And if garou procreate by flings or not. Because the setting loves to flip flop between those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T23:53:55-08:00","id":820787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820641#post820641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before any of that is, we have to first figure out whether pre-change homid garou are raised unaware of their natures, or not. And if garou procreate by flings or not. Because the setting loves to flip flop between those two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the answer would be, if people so removes from garou society, who weren't considered kin anymore (and probably didn't register as kin magically) are now suddenly kin again and potentially garou, then they weren't raised as garou, for they didn't exist just one global spiritual incident ago.<br /> <br /> Regardless if garou can discern pre-changers from kin (like before W20) or not. If no garou ever checked, because it wasn't necessary, then those children couldn't be educated properly. Of course the regular cubs might still be around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:15:26-08:00","id":820798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820641#post820641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before any of that is, we have to first figure out whether pre-change homid garou are raised unaware of their natures, or not. And if garou procreate by flings or not. Because the setting loves to flip flop between those two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about seemingly normal humans just up and ending up changing after having sex and someone getting pregnant. Oops. Alternately, problems cropping up like in Peter Is The Wold, involving accidental bites. Whelp, looks like you can't be with your beloved any more - and in a short enough time, you might not be able to be with anyone, since Garou can't produce lasting lineages with each other. It all relies on enough accidents happening, and the one thing that's sure about accidents is that they will happen. This setting just wasn't made to have so many new Garou show up through a mechanism like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T14:17:54-08:00","id":821206,"title":"","content":"To quote the immortal bard... Hell No.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Apocalypse is its own beast, and it has created its own quirky and weird setting. This whole concept seems to be a cheap excuse to introduce lycantrophy and more adult characters on a whim. Neither of those do anything to Werewolf other then trash core concepts behind them as a group.<br /> <br /> I can see why BNS would want that. &quot;Proper Werewolves&quot; is a hangup for people who have a hard time taking Werewolf on its own merit, and the idea of bites spreading it means you can have a bunch of fresh Werewolves who just turned for lowly first rankers to start their new games.<br /> <br /> I am gonna keep an eye out on what's gonna develop with this, as I'm curious how it will pertain to a future 4th edition of Werewolf, but it's really not something I am interested in seeing in Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T16:44:12-08:00","id":821300,"title":"","content":"People are seriously overstating what's in the gamma slice... BNS isn't introducing lycantrophy into WtA. It's not even WtF's spontaneous Wolf-blooded from exposure to Lunacy.<br /> <br /> Humans and wolves that can turn into Garou from a bite have to have been touched spiritually by something completely out of the Garou's control (and possibly ability to know ahead of time) first. It's a change to the setting... but it's also a change in-setting. This is supposed to be a new phenomenon that's suddenly started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:04:23-08:00","id":821308,"title":"","content":"Please also take note: BNS is still taking suggestions, constructive critiques, and the likes.<br /> IF you have suggestions, and comments please (politely) Email them at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#91f8fff7fed1f3e8fff8f6f9e5e2e5e4f5f8fee2bff2fefc\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"92fbfcf4fdd2f0ebfcfbf5fae6e1e6e7f6fbfde1bcf1fdff\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. They likely won't contact you directly as they're compiling the information and using it in meetings to help make decisions.<br /> <br /> Now, as for &quot;The Bite&quot;, this is all we know so far:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Further, many Theurges speculate that the natural balance is attempting to restore itself, spontaneously evolving werewolf genetics in otherwise normal wolves and humans. Sometimes this potential remains dormant throughout an individual\u2019s life. However, when bitten by a werewolf, the spark can be triggered, resulting in a mutation that rebuilds the individual\u2019s DNA. This mutation causes a debilitating, flu-like sickness that eventually, within a month\u2019s time, results in the First Change. </div> </div> </div>Please note here that all that is presented here are mostly theories. All Garou know is that they're (for some reason) biting people, and for some reason certain people wind up going through a month-long transformation and becoming Garou.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that the idea of folks who are otherwise normal folks who are &quot;bitten&quot; and find themselves becoming Garou is fine. But the idea that Garou are going around biting folks and not killing them (kinky sex?) and then SOME of those people wind up having had a dormant &quot;gift&quot; that is activated by a Garou's supernatural bite and begins a process of turning them into Garou leaves some weirdness.<br /> <br /> My proposed suggestions are going to be this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The current wording of how &quot;otherwise normal wolves and humans&quot; can change into Garou from a bite is odd in that there's no reason why Garou would go around biting folks to find the few who will transform from a bite--this is a huge breach of the veil and causes all sorts of problems. For this reason, I propose reasons why Garou would bite someone:<br /> <br /> 1) Kinfolk with a high-enough Pure Breed (3 or higher) can be bitten and turned into Garou (1 in 10)<br /> 2) Kinfolk can be put through a Rite that can enhance their chances (increasing it to 2 in 10?)<br /> 3) Anyone who turns into a Garou through &quot;The Bite&quot; must take a permanent and irremovable bite scar at the site of the wound. This mark is both physical and spiritual. Those who are bitten and do not turn into Garou receive the same permanent scar.<br /> 4) Each time a Garou successfully creates another werewolf through the Bite, her permanent Gnosis is reduced by one. This makes creating new Garou part of a personal sacrifice, and limits how many a Garou can make through a Bite (this permanent reduction only happens on a successful transformation.)<br /> 5) Keep the idea that a &quot;Bitten&quot; Garou can't make other Garou through a bite.<br /> 6) A newly-bitten Garou becomes the Ward of their &quot;creator&quot; and is spiritually obligated to help help instruct/train them until their Rite of Passage.<br /> <br /> Much of this would be in the history, but allows for the RP of Kinfolk characters who want to become Garou.<br /> This also creates a whole new aspect to the Garou/Kin relationship, as the &quot;best&quot; can be brought up and &quot;attempt&quot; to be given the Gift.<br /> <br /> By doing this, it allows the Garou to be more pro-active in who becomes Garou, choosing the best candidates and hoping their &quot;gift&quot; is true. It makes them accountable.<br /> <br /> Of course, some of this is going to be seen as being too close to Vampire (Sires taking Ghouls and making them into Vampires, etc.) but the same concept goes for any sort of Mentor, even in Mage as well, so why would such a natural concept be out of line for Garou?<br /> <br /> I would also like some sort of story hook where either the Galliards are searching for lore, or Theurges are seeking spirits to help explain what is happening. At least something that shows that there's an answer in the works and could/will be explained in time and not just deus ex machina. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:13:10-08:00","id":821366,"title":"","content":"Flu-like symptoms in otherwise &quot;normal&quot; characters and a month-long change sounds too close to the way that the Ratkin's Birthing Plague works. Also, even if it's in-character speculation, it's fairly widely known that you can't tell Garou from kin by looking at their genes; what separates them is a spiritual matter. Hence, only the least informed Garou would be talking about DNA when it comes to this, and the text doesn't seem to be giving the utterly uninformed the floor for that bit of speculation. This is also the in-universe reason that D.N.A., the medical research corporation, will forever be slamming its head into a brick wall, with no major breakthrough in sight.<br /> <br /> (Posting here as a reminder to myself to write that e-mail message, mostly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:16:18-08:00","id":821397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821366#post821366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div 