 Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to (blessedly sensible) retcons, it doesn't matter, because there isn't one. No protein or pleiotropy hints at the merging of spirit and flesh. Later books had kinfolk and Garou sharing a gene marker set, but this didn't actual code for anything; it was just a red herring for poor, poor D.N.A.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF we can show that it was actually retconned, or canonically proven to be, well, disproven in the setting, this could be shown to the BNS folks as proof that there wasn't a DNA marker that could be found/traced.<br /> <br /> I've tried to hold that I don't mind if it's &quot;genetics&quot;, but I'd rather it be a &quot;spiritual scar&quot; from the brutality of the change than a physical DNA marker that can be tested/shown. Right now, they say &quot;It was in Valkenburg&quot; and if it can be shown otherwise, then that could help change things in the book too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=