 can be tested/shown. Right now, they say &quot;It was in Valkenburg&quot; and if it can be shown otherwise, then that could help change things in the book too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You manged to talk with them about that, or is there a clarification somewhere else about this? And the argument &quot;It was in First Edition&quot; is not a particularly good one with White Wolf games :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T05:38:04-08:00","id":821567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821454#post821454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IF we can show that it was actually retconned, or canonically proven to be, well, disproven in the setting, this could be shown to the BNS folks as proof that there wasn't a DNA marker that could be found/traced.<br /> <br /> I've tried to hold that I don't mind if it's &quot;genetics&quot;, but I'd rather it be a &quot;spiritual scar&quot; from the brutality of the change than a physical DNA marker that can be tested/shown. Right now, they say &quot;It was in Valkenburg&quot; and if it can be shown otherwise, then that could help change things in the book too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If their isnt a Garou Gene then DNA's Efforts should be doomed to failure... and the &quot;Mockery breeds&quot; should not exist... Im not sure how I feel on that, I get a good laugh at the thought of DNA looking for something that doesnt exist... but the mockery breeds are pretty cool...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T06:09:14-08:00","id":821578,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the DNA simply acts as an anchor for the spiritual lineage, and it's the lineage itself they managed to extract. Because magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T06:57:33-08:00","id":821599,"title":"","content":"Mockery Breeds are products of Wyrmish science and melding spirit and flesh. There's little &quot;ordinary&quot; within that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:42:30-08:00","id":821609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821578#post821578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the DNA simply acts as an anchor for the spiritual lineage, and it's the lineage itself they managed to extract. Because magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be little different from having a Garou gene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If their isnt a Garou Gene then DNA's Efforts should be doomed to failure... and the &quot;Mockery breeds&quot; should not exist... Im not sure how I feel on that, I get a good laugh at the thought of DNA looking for something that doesnt exist... but the mockery breeds are pretty cool...</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> DNA's efforts are doomed to failure, as an explicit matter called out by the text. They think that everything about the Garou can be reduced down to a super complex interaction between a system of genes, but they have yet to even explain the changes in mass that occur between each form (which would be an easy thing to detect with gravity anomalies, if not an easy thing to explain). They're putting the cart before the horse because they think that the markers they see on kin are the answer, but we, as readers of the setting, have been informed that the situation is not in their favor. DNA's only major accomplishment is Project Reaper, aka The World's Worst Job and Funding Ragequit.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T07:55:00-08:00","id":821619,"title":"","content":"For lycanthropy to be an inherited trait, there needs to be some manner of &quot;garou gene&quot; on <i>some </i>plane of reality. It's not material, we've established that, but there needs to be some sort of spiritual tag linking an individual to their garou forefathers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:11:05-08:00","id":821628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821619#post821619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For lycanthropy to be an inherited trait, there needs to be some manner of &quot;garou gene&quot; on <i>some </i>plane of reality. It's not material, we've established that, but there needs to be some sort of spiritual tag linking an individual to their garou forefathers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits probably don't need something so pinned down, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:35:28-08:00","id":821639,"title":"","content":"Remember the children of gaia had a rite in 3rd edition that made normal humans Kinfolk, AND Occasionaly normal humans SPONTANEOUS become kinfolk... also A garou with Hathrors blessing (If any exist) can cause ANY Two humans to produce a garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:42:43-08:00","id":821644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821639#post821639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember the children of gaia had a rite in 3rd edition that made normal humans Kinfolk, AND Occasionaly normal humans SPONTANEOUS become kinfolk... also A garou with Hathrors blessing (If any exist) can cause ANY Two humans to produce a garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of Gaia Revised. Really. Really!? How can you even bring that into any serious discussion?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:41:44-08:00","id":821723,"title":"","content":"While I'm not entirely against discarding CoG: Revised, I think there is a point where we either have to accept all the books within the WtA canon and examine the references made on their own merits instead of throwing out books because we don't like them. &quot;There's no precedent in the books, <i>if you ignore all the books that set such precedent</i>.&quot; is a very weak position, even if the books being ignored are generally worth being ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T12:13:57-08:00","id":821797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821723#post821723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not entirely against discarding CoG: Revised, I think there is a point where we either have to accept all the books within the WtA canon and examine the references made on their own merits instead of throwing out books because we don't like them. &quot;There's no precedent in the books, <i>if you ignore all the books that set such precedent</i>.&quot; is a very weak position, even if the books being ignored are generally worth being ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we look into the validity and precedent of the material presented in WOD: Gypsies as well, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T12:42:30-08:00","id":821821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821797#post821797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should we look into the validity and precedent of the material presented in WOD: Gypsies as well, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. Who cares about precedent... we aren't the supreme court. This game isn't a religion, there is no cannon or catechism that must be adhered to lest we be branded heretics. There is plenty of dumb garbage that can and should be ignored in the name of taste and sanity. We are not any poorer for exercising discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T13:27:17-08:00","id":821844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821797#post821797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should we look into the validity and precedent of the material presented in WOD: Gypsies as well, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. The claims of racism in that book, are overhyped. Gypsy mystics are a staple part of the gothic subcultures that CWOD was made to apeal to. Angel in the Buffyverse, was cursed by Gypsys, the protaganist of The Hunchback of Notre Dam rescues a Gypsy. im sorry if it seems racist to real people from the Romani... But some real native Americans didnt Care for Chakotay in Star Trek Voyager. Any thoughts of how the book works MECHANICALLY The powers the gypsys learn etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T14:31:19-08:00","id":821881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821797#post821797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we look into the validity and precedent of the material presented in WOD: Gypsies as well, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which material?<br /> <br /> That's my point. I agree WOD: Gypsies and CoG Revised are bad books. But that doesn't mean everything in them is inherently tainted and beyond use (though the list for WOD: Gypsies is extremely small). Instead of saying, &quot;this is a shitty book, so nothing in it counts,&quot; there should by a consideration of what's actually being cited and whether or not it can be separated from what makes those books bad.<br /> <br /> Otherwise they just become pointless WOD versions of Goodwin's law.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821821#post821821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who cares about precedent... we aren't the supreme court. This game isn't a religion, there is no cannon or catechism that must be adhered to lest we be branded heretics. There is plenty of dumb garbage that can and should be ignored in the name of taste and sanity. We are not any poorer for exercising discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of funny... considering that one of the big complaints about the changes BNS seems to be introducing is for... well following this very advice.<br /> <br /> BNS added something, to a somewhat predictable cry of, &quot;This isn't true WtA!&quot; to which the obvious counterargument of, &quot;well... this actually is in WtA before this, BNS didn't pull it out of their asses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Precedent matters because it changes the debate from, &quot;Is BNS wrong to add this element to the game?&quot; to,&quot;Is BNS wrong to stress this element of the game, esp. as it was significantly reduced over time?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821844#post821844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The claims of racism in that book, are overhyped.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. And stop you're not helping your own argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T21:43:52-08:00","id":822117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821881#post821881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is kind of funny... considering that one of the big complaints about the changes BNS seems to be introducing is for... well following this very advice.<br /> <br /> BNS added something, to a somewhat predictable cry of, &quot;This isn't true WtA!&quot; to which the obvious counterargument of, &quot;well... this actually is in WtA before this, BNS didn't pull it out of their asses.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True enough- but I am not going to be one of those crying, at least not at this early date... the only way BNS will really suck is if there is nothing salvageable at all, which I strongly doubt will be the case.<br /> <br /> Precedent is not something that should be wholly discarded either, you are right... but I would say it should only be used to inform/inspire, not justify stultifying or terrible elements of the setting. Of course what this means will vary from person to person, but hey, that is alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T23:32:49-08:00","id":822163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821567#post821567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If their isnt a Garou Gene then DNA's Efforts should be doomed to failure... and the &quot;Mockery breeds&quot; should not exist... Im not sure how I feel on that, I get a good laugh at the thought of DNA looking for something that doesnt exist... but the mockery breeds are pretty cool...</div> </div> </div> </div>Genetics play a very small part in the overall creation of mockery breeds.<br /> <br /> Edit: And thanks, glad you like them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:16:50-08:00","id":822207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821881#post821881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which material?<br /> <br /> That's my point. I agree WOD: Gypsies and CoG Revised are bad books. But that doesn't mean everything in them is inherently tainted and beyond use (though the list for WOD: Gypsies is extremely small). Instead of saying, &quot;this is a shitty book, so nothing in it counts,&quot; there should by a consideration of what's actually being cited and whether or not it can be separated from what makes those books bad.<br /> <br /> Otherwise they just become pointless WOD versions of Goodwin's law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I get you are coming from a point in which you want to discuss preset concepts and where you want to weigh different approaches to the work. But Children of Gaia Revised is one of the most egregious examples of how much an author can miss the point of the game and still be published thanks to the supplement treadmill of White Wolf of yore. We have been dealing with this on the forums a number of times by now, and each time we were all flabergasted at the material presented within. (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/618440-children-of-gaia-revised-is-it-really-that-bad\">This was the most recent one</a>)<br /> <br /> We are talking about the book that presents the Children of Gaia as...<br /> - reinforcing the worst stereotypes of the tribe<br /> - reinforcing the worst stereotypes of OTHER tribes.<br /> - white liberal flower children who promote intergarou relationships<br /> - handling same sex relationships with the same tact of a freight train<br /> - people claiming the american constitution as a product of CoG meddling and a reintroduction of the first edition horrorshow where half the historical figures in the book are Werewolves and/or helped by CoG?<br /> - about making Caerns in public with thousands of clueless humans there to die horribly when the Wyrm comes<br /> - utter disregard for the concept of the Veil<br /> - werewolves dying from overdose of heroin<br /> - a Lupus who knows who Jesus and Pontius Pilate are<br /> - loving Jesus and some of them feel he may have been &quot;more&quot; then anything Gaian<br /> - a magical hermaphroditic Metis who ended the Impergium<br /> - having zero responsibility for the War of Rage - because the other Garou tricked them!<br /> - utilising sex healing gifts<br /> - The Rite of Clouds and Rain - Group sex in Crinos. Let me repeat that: GROUP SEX IN CRINOS<br /> <br /> The biggest sin of this book is not even the horrifying shitshow, inane fiction and utter crap that went past the radar... It's the fact that it totally ruined a group that's already misunderstood and that needed a good tribebook to make it shine. I mean, look at what the Get of Fenris book did for their tribe!<br /> <br /> At which point do we stop going through all the crap in that book over and over and over and concluding it's not good and has little to do with Werewolf and just cut our losses and start ignoring it for the badness that it is? There are very few books that I actually regret buying. This is one of them. For me, invoking this steaming pile of poo, is pretty much Goodwin's law.<br /> <br /> Especially considering that the Storyteller's Handbook (which came out after this drivel) is a much more balanced and in touch piece that handles a lot of long standing Werewolf questions and responds to them in an even handed, out of character tone, discussing key issues and giving us answers to many questions and problems that came up along the line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:54:24-08:00","id":822226,"title":"","content":"Wasn't this thread about how the new rules for garou biting people makes garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T03:17:43-08:00","id":822236,"title":"","content":"We're discussing the validity of a potential precedent for the phenomenon. It's relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-03-2016, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:34:25-08:00","id":822420,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much lost that relevance to a pointless rehash of things we already know as a dodge of the point being made though. Asmodai has made it clear that if you reference CoG: Revised, you lose automatically no matter how good your point is or is not, which pretty much makes this tangent meaningless since it was invoked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:54:52-08:00","id":822437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=822420#post822420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty much lost that relevance to a pointless rehash of things we already know as a dodge of the point being made though. Asmodai has made it clear that if you reference CoG: Revised, you lose automatically no matter how good your point is or is not, which pretty much makes this tangent meaningless since it was invoked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey. I said that invoking CoG Revised is a non argument, as my obviously bitter and acidic post points out, that particular book is a big red button for me. That does not mean that the rest of the topic is meritless. But start with something more sensible for details on Werewolf genetics and genesis... like the Valkenburg Foundation and Samuel Haight (and I'm not invoking the latter lightly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:07:08-08:00","id":822445,"title":"","content":"Alright, so Haight as he was originally conceived (and subsequently trimmed back to in W20) was simply a kinfolk man who discovered a way to effectively supercharge his Garou heritage to the point where it fully activated. That in and of itself doesn't seem too bad, especially considering the complexity of the ritual required to do it.<br /> <br /> From there it doesn't seem <i>too</i> far fetched that another ritual could have similar results, implanting a seed of power that awaits a specific trigger, in this case a bite from a garou. Presumably this would be a one-off event. Eventually everyone so affected would either have changed or died, and the status quo on how new garou arise would be restored. *shrug*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:51:35-08:00","id":822472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=822445#post822445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so Haight as he was originally conceived (and subsequently trimmed back to in W20) was simply a kinfolk man who discovered a way to effectively supercharge his Garou heritage to the point where it fully activated. That in and of itself doesn't seem too bad, especially considering the complexity of the ritual required to do it.<br /> <br /> From there it doesn't seem <i>too</i> far fetched that another ritual could have similar results, implanting a seed of power that awaits a specific trigger, in this case a bite from a garou. Presumably this would be a one-off event. Eventually everyone so affected would either have changed or died, and the status quo on how new garou arise would be restored. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't supercharge it, he stole the power of five other Garou by killing them and taking their skins. You can theoretically have five Garou willingly give up their lives to the same effect sans taint, but the exchange rate isn't going to get any better. Even the Birthing Plague, the one fixture of Werewolf that looks anything like the &quot;infection&quot; model of therianthropy in fiction, usually kills the ones that infects. If the way the Kitsune work is anything to go by, the best you could get would be &quot;kill about nine humans through breed-theme appropriate means to make one Kinfolk into a full Garou&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:53:10-08:00","id":822473,"title":"","content":"The ritual only works on kinfolk though, right? So some sort of spark is required to fan into a full flame.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I see what you mean. There was a net decrease of garou there. So presumably whatever caused this would need some other power source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-03-2016, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:56:47-08:00","id":822571,"title":"","content":"I like Sam Haight... as a Bitter and cynical man who was determined to prove himself more then his garou cousins thought of him. And managed to achieve great power and near godhood...Never the less... I hate the whole &quot;magic staff with all the powers of an archmage&quot; thing, as much as anyone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:57:59-08:00","id":822573,"title":"","content":"also kinfolk unsung heroes references (Without rules) Occasional cases where normal humans SPONTANEOUSLY become kinfolk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:01:47-08:00","id":822725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=822437#post822437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does not mean that the rest of the topic is meritless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring to the tangent on which books to reference, nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T07:32:18-08:00","id":823329,"title":"","content":"I don't have a stake in this argument, I don't LARP and I have no real feelings on the bite subject. But I have witnessed LARP in action and old White Wolf at that it was large short of every LARP being set at a Grand Moot given the numbers of Garou mentioned it makes business sense for BNS to have an explanation for the sheer number of Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T11:58:46-08:00","id":823575,"title":"","content":"Another point on practical LARPing, is that a lot of LARP groups (and similarly large gaming organizations like chats) are 18+ for CYA legal reasons given the material of the games. Having more reasons to have older (by WtA standards) Cliaths is another reason for BNS to change things up in this direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:03:16-08:00","id":823939,"title":"","content":"I can agree with how this stuff can help out a LARP with population and 18+ players. If that's the case then I hope it stays LARP specific, it doesn't need to push over to table top then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:18:36-08:00","id":823949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=823939#post823939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can agree with how this stuff can help out a LARP with population and 18+ players. If that's the case then I hope it stays LARP specific, it doesn't need to push over to table top then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, while it will not affect the books, a lot of online players are LARPers and so a lot of larp stuff ends up in the games. Like having to buy lore for your own tribe of knowledge of garou in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:57:57-08:00","id":823965,"title":"","content":"Oh another reference... when I was on Starwars Fanfiction forums nearly 2 decades ago, in the late 90s (Before the relase of phantom menace) I saw a post of &quot;Many things, including the existence of the Ewoks, is not cannon&quot; I think the reason was because the ewoks dare to be CUTE and worse to topple the imperials in spite of their cutenesss.... just an anecdote I thought of... these days not as big on star wars, so little interest now that the EU's been decannonized, that ive decided not to even watch &quot;the force awakens&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:05:44-08:00","id":824006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=821469#post821469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf Revised Storyteller's Handbook page 20, the first item in the FAQ.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to try to find that and submit it to see if it can loosen their grip on the whole &quot;Garou DNA&quot; bit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:59:06-08:00","id":824063,"title":"","content":"Latecomer to this particular debate, and my whole opinion of the &quot;possible mutations that let you play as lycanthrope&quot; thing is...<br /> <br /> Ambivalent. But not really.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I absolutely hate it. I hate its implication. Random shmucks suddenly get bit and awaken their super-secret, incredibly distant Garou heritage? Garou just don't work that way. And if they did, and if Gaia could have always made that possible, why wait until <b>after</b> a near-earth-ending Sorta-Apocalypse? Wouldn't you have called in these potential reinforcements to <b>stop</b> the Times of Terribadness? Maybe <b>avert</b> the Pseudo-pocalyse??<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, my group are mostly VtM players who want to try a WtA game. But a couple people have trouble making members of one of the tribes. Maybe something like this, an option to start off as an adult just coming into Garou culture, could work for them.<br /> <br /> But in the end, both hands kind of throw themselves in the air until they hold a WtA 4e book in them, so I can see if that's the way the table top game goes and how they fully work it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:12:09-08:00","id":824072,"title":"","content":"The option of starting off as an adult was always there. The Late change is a thing. Couple that with the fact that some septs may need years before they get a pack for a cub, and you could easily have low ranks with higher age brackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T02:33:08-08:00","id":824131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824063#post824063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou just don't work that way. And if they did, and if Gaia could have always made that possible, why wait until <b>after</b> a near-earth-ending Sorta-Apocalypse? Wouldn't you have called in these potential reinforcements to <b>stop</b> the Times of Terribadness? Maybe <b>avert</b> the Pseudo-pocalyse??</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou <b>didn't</b> work that way. This is an explicit new phenomenon in the setting.<br /> <br /> And we don't have any real details about how it happened, or why, so there's a lot of mixed charity in responses to how those questions might be answered. The BNS gamma slice, and some of the teasers from WWP about their ideas for W4, indicate that whatever happened with the Red Star there are two things:<br /> <br /> First the Garou consider the &quot;now&quot; the Age of the Apocalypse. Whatever huge disaster of battles that happened between Revised and now was the first stage, not the end. This means that it makes perfect sense for now to be the time for Gaia to start pulling out the stops. Her army just took massive loses, and the war isn't over. So those numbers need bolstering like never before.<br /> <br /> Second, Gaia is apparent out of the picture now. It's not clear if whatever happened killed her (if that's even possible) as a functional entity, or she left for whatever mystical reasons. Whatever she did to change the status quo of the Garou before the current &quot;now&quot; is going to be her parting impact before leaving the board. Hell, it's possible the only reason she did it now is doing so would mean her inability to take any further direct actions on her warriors' behalf, so she figured she was getting taken out anyway, so might as well.<br /> <br /> There's nothing wrong with these questions not getting direct answers either. The setting could use some mystery, and why the hell this his happening now instead of before it got this bad is an excellent mystery for players to explore if they want to. Maybe chip away at the Garou's long standing certainty in their goddess by having her hold something like this back for long. Maybe reinforce that bond as dying gifts from her enter the world before she departs. Lots of options, lots of hooks, all are things to play with, rather than worry about out-of-character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824072#post824072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The option of starting off as an adult was always there. The Late change is a thing. Couple that with the fact that some septs may need years before they get a pack for a cub, and you could easily have low ranks with higher age brackets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> Been around this enough times it really ends up feeling forced. &quot;95% of homids have their first change between 14-16, but 100% of PC are either late changes, or took years to train completely,&quot; just gets annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:01:35-08:00","id":824140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824131#post824131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, Gaia is apparent out of the picture now. It's not clear if whatever happened killed her (if that's even possible) as a functional entity, or she left for whatever mystical reasons. Whatever she did to change the status quo of the Garou before the current &quot;now&quot; is going to be her parting impact before leaving the board. Hell, it's possible the only reason she did it now is doing so would mean her inability to take any further direct actions on her warriors' behalf, so she figured she was getting taken out anyway, so might as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia has been out of the picture and not responding to the Garou through the whole game line. It's one of the big things in Werewolf, and what terrifies them. The idea that she suddenly comes and changes the whole way the Garou work and is still gone is a bit iffy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824131#post824131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been around this enough times it really ends up feeling forced. &quot;95% of homids have their first change between 14-16, but 100% of PC are either late changes, or took years to train completely,&quot; just gets annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the game was made, the idea was that it should resonate with the target audience. The whole teenage years thing has been getting looser and looser through the editions. With the fact that most of us playing it have gotten quite a bit older and are still playing it. The good thing is that it only said the majority changed in their adolescence. You can still play older people, and that's probably quite common considering the fact that you are not banned from taking Knowledges, limited in skills or forced to play a &quot;child&quot;, which is a Flaw of its own. It doesn't have to be 95%, it could be 55% or 70% too.<br /> <br /> The latter books are intentionaly vague, I happen to have Revised at hand at work, so I can actually quote this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf Revised</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, some time after adolescence, a young werewolf undergoes his First Change.<br /> This event is often brought on by stress or trauma, leading the confused young werewolf to lash out at whatever is hurting him.<br /> ...<br /> Regardless of age, the \u201ccub\u201d is treated like a child until she decides to accept her destiny and join the community of the Garou.<br /> ...<br /> You can create a character from any nation, of any age, from any cultural background, but your character has undergone the First Change only recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:12:40-08:00","id":824144,"title":"","content":"Yes, the option to be any age as change has been around for a while as a lost cub or late bloomer. Now the LARP system has another, newer option to use additionally along side that. One with more options for stories of all those non-puberty Garou running around. Chosen by garou, Accident, act of violence, BSD shovelhead.<br /> <br /> Garou genes and measurements or spirituality????<br /> <br /> As above by Saur Ops, Storytellers guide, page 20. Really not hard to find at all. It is the first question and answer in the FAQ.<br /> <b>&quot;Is there such a thing as a &quot;Garou gene?&quot; Can it be detected with DNA analysis? Can werewolves be cloned?</b><br /> Not really, no.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because Gaia chooses. She chooses them from birth, it's her choice.<br /> <br /> Page 204 players guide has a bit about kinfolk too and being a relative.<br /> <br /> &quot;If someone is related to a werewolf, is he automatically Kinfolk? What about genetics? Usually, but not always. Being Kin is not just a matter of blood ties; it\u2019s also spiritual. Gaia knows who She wants mingling with Her warriors. She may choose to bless a distantly related human with Kin blood while a direct descendent of a werewolf may not be Kin at all.&quot;<br /> <br /> Key words to me &quot;Gaia knows who she wants&quot;<br /> <br /> The interesting thing to me about all this biting business is that now those who will of Gaia's chosen (you've heard that term before right), are now no longer just 'Her' chosen. Garou get to pick and chose, BSDs get to go crazy with it and possibly turn whole little communities. Is it still Gaia's choice? did she give the ability to her children to do it? or is there something even bigger or perhaps diabolical behind it all? Maybe it's the Wyld in its latest rolling acts of chaos trolling the universe?<br /> <br /> I don't really like the idea of the Garou becoming vampire like in their blessings and sacrifice to Gaia. It lacks the whole natural feel and closeness to nature they have in ...well..breeding. Creating life, in the hopes of continuing it. That and the difficulties in having to wait for nearly a couple of decades (yes, I know lupus don't take as long, you know this, I know this, we all know, stop being pernickety) to see if one will be the next hero Gaia needs. But it does create new options and possibilities for other players to explore, some might not be liked,some might be frowned upon, others mihght be embraced or marvelled at in a LARP community. So although not a fan, I look forwards to seeing and hearing about what players are doing with this new opportunity, but mostly...what the STs and Writers are planning to do with it.<br /> <br /> Is it Gaia's will to pass this ability to the Garou? If not, where did it come from? What other changes may come? What new dangers might the nation face from this 'outbreak'? In Garou Heirarchy...who gets to choose and act to recruit? Will the Tribal Totems be connected to those bitten? How will the Totems feel about those bitten and not Gaia Chosen? What if the Bite's affects dont last forever or fluctuates/wanes/slumbers/remiss' at certain times? What if a Garou chooses someone but their totem wont accept them or another Tribe challenges for them? and that's just off the top my head, so I imagine the writers have a lot more in mind for down the line. I might not like it, but I bet others will and have fun with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:26:27-08:00","id":824336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824063#post824063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the one hand, I absolutely hate it. I hate its implication. Random shmucks suddenly get bit and awaken their super-secret, incredibly distant Garou heritage? Garou just don't work that way. And if they did, and if Gaia could have always made that possible, why wait until <b>after</b> a near-earth-ending Sorta-Apocalypse? Wouldn't you have called in these potential reinforcements to <b>stop</b> the Times of Terribadness? Maybe <b>avert</b> the Pseudo-pocalyse??</div> </div> </div> </div>Who the hell are you to question Mama Gaia? The Garou Nation gets a shot in the arm and you whine because it didn't happen earlier? :P<br /> <br /> I am only half kidding. Blaming the gods of a setting for not being proactive enough is silly They can't really do all that much directly, meta-narratively speaking, because if they did the setting would not be about what Gaia's children, the Garou, accomplish, it would be about whatever world-shattering thing the Celestines and Triat are up to. The Greek gods were weak so that heroes like Hercules and Orpheus can do cool stuff without being overshadowed by the fantastic doings of the deities.<br /> <br /> From a WtA standpoint, pick a reason why it did not happen sooner. Maybe the Mother was hurt so badly in the Unpocalypse that in her agony she has started to lash out and spontaneously create more defenders. Maybe there is more at work here than just Gaia waking up one day and making humans into Garou. Maybe it required the cooperation of other spirits- the Weaver may have offered its blessing in allowing apes to become wolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 02-05-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:07:27-08:00","id":824359,"title":"","content":"&quot;Maybe there's more at work here?&quot; The Laughing Stranger.<br /> <br /> agreed. I like to think so, especially if it does cross over to WtA. Not that I necessarily want it too.<br /> <br /> and coming up with individual and Tribal reaaons as to why it's happening could also be quite enjoyable. Especially if later the answer, or reason does come to light (Quests, so many quests for knowledge!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T10:04:01-08:00","id":824402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824336#post824336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who the hell are you to question Mama Gaia? The Garou Nation gets a shot in the arm and you whine because it didn't happen earlier? :P<br /> <br /> I am only half kidding. Blaming the gods of a setting for not being proactive enough is silly They can't really do all that much directly, meta-narratively speaking, because if they did the setting would not be about what Gaia's children, the Garou, accomplish, it would be about whatever world-shattering thing the Celestines and Triat are up to. The Greek gods were weak so that heroes like Hercules and Orpheus can do cool stuff without being overshadowed by the fantastic doings of the deities.<br /> <br /> From a WtA standpoint, pick a reason why it did not happen sooner. Maybe the Mother was hurt so badly in the Unpocalypse that in her agony she has started to lash out and spontaneously create more defenders. Maybe there is more at work here than just Gaia waking up one day and making humans into Garou. Maybe it required the cooperation of other spirits- the Weaver may have offered its blessing in allowing apes to become wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I can't accept the whole bit about the gods not acting directly in-setting... Because this seems a pretty direct change. A big, huge one, and made from a god-thing that's been described as on the verge of dying, if not already dead, since WtA1e. And all because her champions were too few in numbers.<br /> <br /> If I were dying because, say, my white blood cell count was low and I had some way to suddenly increase that white blood cell count by allowing my red blood cells to transform into whites, I doubt I'd wait until the last minute to pull that trigger. And really, that's the closest analogy I can think of.<br /> <br /> All that said, as I mentioned in my initial post, I'm gonna wait and see how it works out in 4e, if it's even included, before really saying if I find it to be a terrible idea (or just terrible execution).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:47:05-08:00","id":824605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824140#post824140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia has been out of the picture and not responding to the Garou through the whole game line. It's one of the big things in Werewolf, and what terrifies them. The idea that she suddenly comes and changes the whole way the Garou work and is still gone is a bit iffy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of.<br /> <br /> While Gaia hasn't bothered to talk to the Garou in ages and all, she has a whole spirit court of her direct avatars and their servants who do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The latter books are intentionaly vague, I happen to have Revised at hand at work, so I can actually quote this: </div> </div> </div>You don't need to quote, because you're ignoring the point:<br /> <br /> The books are written with TT in mind, where you have 3-8 players, and a mix of the Breeds. Metis and Lupus aren't a problem, leaving the homid players not feeling forced/redundant in be exceptions to their normal ages of first change<br /> <br /> When you're dealing with 40 players? That doesn't work. You can't have 40 characters that are all special snowflakes in-character and maintain the idea that such things are supposed to be rare/exceptions to the rule. There's a pressure for the PCs to mirror &quot;normal&quot; distributions of things like Breeds (so less Lupus and Metis than homids), and stick closer to &quot;normal&quot; ranges of when major life events are supposed to happen.<br /> <br /> If I have five PCs in my game, they can be outliers to the norm, and I have a whole Sept of NPCs to reinforce norms with. In a LARP style situation, the PCs are going to be the majority of the Sept, so I can't just toss in 10 NPCs for every PC to re-establish the &quot;normal&quot; of the setting (because then I have 200+ Garou in a Sept which is an entirely different change of things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:51:43-08:00","id":824607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824402#post824402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I were dying because, say, my white blood cell count was low and I had some way to suddenly increase that white blood cell count by allowing my red blood cells to transform into whites, I doubt I'd wait until the last minute to pull that trigger. And really, that's the closest analogy I can think of.</div> </div> </div> </div>My whole point is that maybe She can't spontaneously protect Herself. It seems uncharitable to assume there is no rationale or in-universe justification for such a change. Maybe there is more happening here than 'BAM! Werewolves are now made with bites sometimes because Gaia said so.'<br /> <br /> Why would you just assume it is a Deus Ex Machina and nothing more? If it is, yes, that would be dumb... but I have a sneaking suspicion the real story is more complex and interesting. As you say, time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:25:29-08:00","id":824657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824607#post824607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My whole point is that maybe She can't spontaneously protect Herself. It seems uncharitable to assume there is no rationale or in-universe justification for such a change. Maybe there is more happening here than 'BAM! Werewolves are now made with bites sometimes because Gaia said so.'<br /> <br /> Why would you just assume it is a Deus Ex Machina and nothing more? If it is, yes, that would be dumb... but I have a sneaking suspicion the real story is more complex and interesting. As you say, time will tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that because what we know is that suddenly, Gaia did it. Way late in the game. Either directly before the Quasi-Apocalypse or right after. My assumption isn't coming out of nowhere, it's acknowledging all the facts to date and making a judgment on them. I mean sure, it's fun to try and predict what this all <i>might </i>morph into, but that's neither here nor there, nor is it what I was addressing at all. I was addressing my personal view on the whole brand new semi-lycanthopy in WtA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T16:27:16-08:00","id":824659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824605#post824605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of.<br /> <br /> While Gaia hasn't bothered to talk to the Garou in ages and all, she has a whole spirit court of her direct avatars and their servants who do.</div> </div> </div> </div>She technically can't talk to Garou directly, because she's greater than a Celestine, and Celestines have to squeeze themselves into avatars in order to communicate with anything smaller than an Incarna. So, the influence from the avatars is pretty much going to be the most direct that you're going to get without turning a character into an Incarna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need to quote, because you're ignoring the point:<br /> <br /> The books are written with TT in mind, where you have 3-8 players, and a mix of the Breeds. Metis and Lupus aren't a problem, leaving the homid players not feeling forced/redundant in be exceptions to their normal ages of first change<br /> <br /> When you're dealing with 40 players? That doesn't work. You can't have 40 characters that are all special snowflakes in-character and maintain the idea that such things are supposed to be rare/exceptions to the rule. There's a pressure for the PCs to mirror &quot;normal&quot; distributions of things like Breeds (so less Lupus and Metis than homids), and stick closer to &quot;normal&quot; ranges of when major life events are supposed to happen.<br /> <br /> If I have five PCs in my game, they can be outliers to the norm, and I have a whole Sept of NPCs to reinforce norms with. In a LARP style situation, the PCs are going to be the majority of the Sept, so I can't just toss in 10 NPCs for every PC to re-establish the &quot;normal&quot; of the setting (because then I have 200+ Garou in a Sept which is an entirely different change of things). </div> </div> </div>If we're going for LARP-based meta-text reasoning, it would probably be better to assume that there were more Garou and Fera from the get-go and not deal with metaplot-related reasons for there being more of them. That way, you can adapt the historical supplements without giant, jarring changes. In any case, &quot;let's do something that, at best, makes the Garou more like another kind of Fera, and at worst more like vampires&quot; is not a good way to go about it. Harrowing journeys into the spirit world by seemingly random people who find strange doorways past the Gauntlet sounds like it might be better to make non-Garou into Garou. Or that I've been playing too much Diablo 3, either one.<br /> <br /> And also, to stop talking about the Garou's nucleotide sequences, because it seems hard to overstate how much of a problem that gets to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T23:27:03-08:00","id":824846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824659#post824659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're going for LARP-based meta-text reasoning, it would probably be better to assume that there were more Garou and Fera from the get-go and not deal with metaplot-related reasons for there being more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just that there are more of them (the meta-plot in the gamma slice is really less about having their be more total Garou in the current era than the Revised era, but about having them more strongly clustered in specific territories instead of smaller Sept all over the place), but meta-text reasoning on <i>older</i> average ages for starting Garou. More lost cubs, more humans with a weird spark that lets them become Garou if bitten by a Garou, etc. increases the average age of starting PCs, which makes it easier on a player base that is generally older as well as avenues of play that are often 18+ (both for players and their characters to not be portraying things with minors in either case).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, &quot;let's do something that, at best, makes the Garou more like another kind of Fera, and at worst more like vampires&quot; is not a good way to go about it. </div> </div> </div>That's not really a factual statement. &quot;Bite turned&quot; Garou going through something similar to the Birthing Plague doesn't actually have an inherent problems. It also doesn't make them more like vampires because they can't bite anyone and turn them into Garou. It's only special people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And also, to stop talking about the Garou's nucleotide sequences, because it seems hard to overstate how much of a problem that gets to be. </div> </div> </div>In out-of-character text? Absolutely. Though it should be noted that this was something that was stated as at least partially in-character speculation. Just because we know that Garou DNA doesn't exist doesn't mean all characters buy that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T07:13:33-08:00","id":824928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=824846#post824846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not just that there are more of them (the meta-plot in the gamma slice is really less about having their be more total Garou in the current era than the Revised era, but about having them more strongly clustered in specific territories instead of smaller Sept all over the place), but meta-text reasoning on <i>older</i> average ages for starting Garou. More lost cubs, more humans with a weird spark that lets them become Garou if bitten by a Garou, etc. increases the average age of starting PCs, which makes it easier on a player base that is generally older as well as avenues of play that are often 18+ (both for players and their characters to not be portraying things with minors in either case).</div> </div> </div> </div>It still seems easier to do that from a returned start than to add it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not really a factual statement. &quot;Bite turned&quot; Garou going through something similar to the Birthing Plague doesn't actually have an inherent problems. It also doesn't make them more like vampires because they can't bite anyone and turn them into Garou. It's only special people. </div> </div> </div>Just like how vampires look only for the people useful to them. A story shifted by degrees. It does make it more about heritage, but so did being an incestuous Venetian necromancer-gangster, back in the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In out-of-character text? Absolutely. Though it should be noted that this was something that was stated as at least partially in-character speculation. Just because we know that Garou DNA doesn't exist doesn't mean all characters buy that. </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that they mostly know by now, since DNA (the organization) keeps rearing its ugly head and that someone is going to explain just why it is that they perpetually never get what they're looking for. Besides, most of the Garou probably wouldn't even give time to think about the concept as relevant in their day to day lives or as speculation for for anything that heavily involves spirits (as their coming into being does). The only ones who probably consider it deeply are Glass Walkers, and they probably also know better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T09:33:41-08:00","id":833346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/820426-spontaneous-werewolf-genetics?p=820469#post820469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I've disliked for a while is the fact that NOTHING Can allow a normal human however worthy to become garou, but in spite of the aforementioned, I accept sometimes life isnt fair, and this creates some fascinating story arcs.<br /> <br /> Id agree this kind of major change is something to VERY CAREFULLY Consider...</div> </div> </div> </div>You forget the Skindancers... but that means finding a bunch of old Werewolfs that want to pass along their pelts to a really worthy or being wyrm-tainted. But the &quot;bite me, make me werewolf&quot; thing is outright ridiculous imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T11:42:27-08:00","id":833415,"title":"","content":"Well, there was always options like the Kami for truly outstandingly worthy people getting a power-up.<br /> <br /> That said, it's worth noting (again) that the BNS stuff is no, &quot;bite me, make me a werewolf.&quot; It is, &quot;some people are latent Garou that need to be woken up, and biting them is the level of trauma - and perhaps proximity to the spiritual essence of a Garou - needed to do so.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T15:50:08-08:00","id":833564,"title":"","content":"I agree about &quot;hell no!&quot; for two reasons:<br /> Firstly, when a Garou bites someone, it's a reasonably clear implication that they want that someone dead. Considering humans can't soak lethal and aggravated damage and most Garou will want to finish the job (because Veil), the chances of surviving a Garou encounter once the first bite has landed are... near zero? Combine that with the human needing to be one of the special few with an active &quot;might become a Garou&quot; marker and maybe you'd get one or two werewolves per year this way - globally. And that's probably already on the high side.<br /> And secondly, infecting people with lycanthropy (or arouanthropy) is the Ratkin's shtick. Translating that to werewolves raises some rather odd questions ingame...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T17:00:42-08:00","id":833591,"title":"","content":"&quot;Raises some rather odd questions in-game&quot; is part of the point though. It forces the Garou to question their SOP of killing humans when it's more convenient than other methods because they might be a Garou. It creates an in-game mystery of can those individuals be found and bitten &quot;safely&quot; or not, and a race to try to find them before the BSDs do.<br /> <br /> I also reject the idea that the Birthing Plague is so essential to the Ratkin that this somehow irrevocably detracts from their themes; esp. as there are some significant differences between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T07:25:12-07:00","id":880958,"title":"","content":"Oh this thread gave me an idea?<br /> <br /> saw a line in Hammer and klaive about how &quot;Gaia NEEDS champions that challenge the gods&quot; So... while it may be presumptious or even blasphemous...<br /> <br /> HEretical gift<br /> <br /> Adoption of the Favored Brother<br /> <br /> Rank 6 (Metis/ Maybe theruge, or possibly silver Fang, as who better to Recognize someone who would be worthy of the Gift of Rage.<br /> <br /> The Garou must spend 4 Permanent Gnosis and 2 Permanent Rage in Advance, then he attacks a human and delivers a nonfatal bite.<br /> <br /> over the next lunar cycle they'll have bizzare dreams acting out, etc, concluding, in some confrontation with a First Change.<br /> <br /> Auspice is determined by the moon the gift is used in.<br /> <br /> and the attack should be conducted in accordance with the moon in question.<br /> <br /> The Full moon is all out frontal assault that miraculously winds up not killing or permanently injuring the Subject.<br /> <br /> The Gibbuous moon Resounds with a Boisterous approach Singing a song, that though the subject does not yet know it, is of the great deeds, he will surely soon be a part of.<br /> <br /> Unsure on Half Moon.<br /> <br /> Crescent moon frequently traps with riddles,or traps in a maze.<br /> <br /> New Moon makes an attack from Stealth Often times not being seen or noticed till the firsting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from the idea itself is the cost too high or low? Wanted it just slightly higher then for Corax, as Garou werent MEANT to propagate in this fashion.<br /> <br /> But always felt it was a weakness that the garou unlike cainites cant adopt those they find worthy.<br /> <br /> I do agree it strongly breaks the settings themes why I acknowledged its heretical just creating it as an idea for those who want such an optioni.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-03-2016, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}